[{"category":"section","location":"useful/#available-operations","page":"Available Operations","text":"using Quantikz # hide\n[P(1), H(2), Id(3), U(4), U(raw\"\\mathrm{Gate}\",5)]\n\nlatexmatrix = raw\"\\begin{pmatrix}\n\\alpha & \\beta \\\\\n\\gamma & \\delta\n\\end{pmatrix}\"\nU(latexmatrix,1)\n\n[CNOT(1,2), CPHASE(2,3), SWAP(3,4)]","title":"Standard Single- and Two-qubit Gates"},{"category":"section","location":"useful/#Multi-Qubit-Gates","page":"Available Operations","text":"","title":"Multi Qubit Gates"},{"category":"section","location":"useful/#Arbitrary-combination-of-filled-circle,-open-circle,-NOT,-and-cross","page":"Available Operations","text":"MultiControl([1],[2],[3],[4])","title":"Arbitrary combination of filled circle, open circle, NOT, and cross"},{"category":"section","location":"useful/#Arbitrary-controlled-gate","page":"Available Operations","text":"[\n    MultiControlU([1], [2], [3,4]),\n    MultiControlU(\"XYZ\",  [1], [2], [3,4,5]),\n    MultiControlU(\"U_a\",  [1], [2], [3,5]),\n]","title":"Arbitrary controlled gate"},{"category":"section","location":"useful/#Gate-dependent-on-classical-bits","page":"Available Operations","text":"[\n    ClassicalDecision(1, 1),\n    ClassicalDecision(\"U\",  [1,2], 2),\n    ClassicalDecision(\"U_a\",  [1,3], [1,3]),\n]","title":"Gate dependent on classical bits"},{"category":"section","location":"useful/#Measurements","page":"Available Operations","text":"","title":"Measurements"},{"category":"section","location":"useful/#Single-qubit,-with-optional-result-stored-to-bits","page":"Available Operations","text":"[\n    Measurement(1),\n    Measurement(\"X\", 2),\n    Measurement(\"Z\", 3, 1)\n]","title":"Single qubit, with optional result stored to bits"},{"category":"section","location":"useful/#Multiple-qubits-stabilizer-measurement,-with-optional-result-stored-to-bits.","page":"Available Operations","text":"[\n    Measurement([1,2]),\n    Measurement(\"ZZ\", [2,3]),\n    Measurement(\"XX\", [3,4], 1)\n]","title":"Multiple qubits stabilizer measurement, with optional result stored to bits."},{"category":"section","location":"useful/#Multiqubit-Bell-measurements","page":"Available Operations","text":"ParityMeasurement([\"X\",\"Y\",\"Z\"], [1,2,4])","title":"Multiqubit Bell measurements"},{"category":"section","location":"useful/#Initial-states-or-resets","page":"Available Operations","text":"","title":"Initial states or resets"},{"category":"section","location":"useful/#At-the-beginning-of-a-circuit","page":"Available Operations","text":"Initialize(\"\\\\ket{\\\\phi}\", [1,2,3])\n\nInitialize(\"\\\\ket{\\\\phi}\", [1,2,4])","title":"At the beginning of a circuit"},{"category":"section","location":"useful/#Midway-through-a-circuit","page":"Available Operations","text":"[CNOT(1,2), Measurement(3), Initialize(\"\\\\ket{\\\\phi}\", [2,3])]\n\n[CNOT(1,2), Measurement(1), Measurement(3), Initialize(\"\\\\ket{\\\\phi}\", [1,3])]","title":"Midway through a circuit"},{"category":"section","location":"useful/#Noise-Events","page":"Available Operations","text":"[Noise([1,5]), NoiseAll()]","title":"Noise Events"},{"category":"section","location":"#Quantikz.jl","page":"Quantikz.jl","text":"A minimal package for drawing quantum circuits using the quantikz[1] and tikz TeX libraries. See an online interactive demo at quantikz.krastanov.org.\n\n[1]: Tutorial on the Quantikz Package, Alastair Kay","title":"Quantikz.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Examples","page":"Quantikz.jl","text":"See the full list of available operations.\n\nusing Quantikz\ncircuit = [\n    CNOT(1,2), CPHASE(2,3), SWAP(3,4),\n    H(5), P(6), Id(7),\n    U(\"\\\\frac{\\\\phi}{4}\",8),\n    Measurement(\"X\",1), Measurement([2,3],2), ClassicalDecision(\"U\",[3,5],2),\n    Measurement(\"M\",[5,6],1),\n    MultiControlU(\"G\",[2,8],[7,3],[4,5,6])]","title":"Examples"},{"category":"section","location":"#Saving-files","page":"Quantikz.jl","text":"Use savecircuit(circuit, filename) for tex, pdf, and png files.","title":"Saving files"},{"category":"section","location":"#Custom-quantikz-TeX-code","page":"Quantikz.jl","text":"For each circuit you can get the quantikz table if you want to modify it.\n\nqtable = circuit2table([CNOT(1,2), CPHASE(2,3)])\nqtable.qubits, qtable.ancillaries, qtable.bits\n\nqtable.table\n\nAnd after modifications, the table can be turned into a tex string\n\ntable2string(qtable)","title":"Custom quantikz TeX code"},{"category":"section","location":"#Custom-Objects","page":"Quantikz.jl","text":"For your CustomQuantumOperation simply define a QuantikzOp(op::CustomQuantumOperation) that converts your object to one of the built-in objects from the examples above.\n\nIf you need more freedom for your custom quantum operation, simply define:\n\nupdate_table!(table,step,op::CustomQuantumOperation) that directly modifies the quantikz table\naffectedqubits(op::CustomQuantumOperation) that gives the indices of qubits involved in the operation.\n(optional) affectedbits(op) that gives the indices of classical bits in use (empty by default)\n(optional) neededancillaries(op) that gives the number of temporary ancillary qubits to reserve (0 by default)\n(optional) nsteps(op) that gives the number of steps involved in the gate (1 by default)\n(optional) deleteoutputs(op) that gives which qubits to be deleted, e.g., their lines removed (empty by default)\n\nInstead of returning an array of indices affectedqubits can also return the lazy slice ibegin:iend (from EndpointRanges.jl) which tells the layout engine that all qubits are used in this stage of the circuit.","title":"Custom Objects"},{"category":"section","location":"API/#Full-API-(autogenerated)","page":"Full API (autogenerated)","text":"","title":"Full API (autogenerated)"},{"category":"module","location":"API/#Quantikz.Quantikz","page":"Full API (autogenerated)","text":"A module for drawing quantum circuits through the Quantikz latex package.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Quantikz.Quantikz"},{"category":"method","location":"API/#Quantikz.explicit_extrema-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Full API (autogenerated)","text":"Turn implicit endpoints to explicit integer indices and take the extrema\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Quantikz.explicit_extrema"},{"category":"method","location":"API/#Quantikz.explicit_targets-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Full API (autogenerated)","text":"Turn implicit endpoints to explicit integer indices\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Quantikz.explicit_targets"}]
